   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Stéphane,<div><br></div><div>The issue here appears to be incompatible BioC versions. Notice the paths generated:</div><div><br></div><div>    <i style=\"font-size:13px\"><a href=\"http://bioconductor.org/packages/2.14/bioc/bin/windows/contrib/3.0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://bioconductor.org/packages/2.14/bioc/bin/windows/contrib/3.0&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242674088000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2lNcWbi6Rdh3PnLqBigDei\">http://bioconductor.org/packages/2.14/bioc/bin/windows/contrib/3.0</a></i></div><div><br></div><div>The base comes from Packrat, and has 2.14, but is completed with 3.0. I imagine this is because we are seeing an incorrect version of BiocInstaller on the path?</div><div><br></div><div>I think a fix would involve us manually constructing these URLs, I think, and only respecting what we see in the Packrat lockfile -- but let me know if you can think of a local workaround as well.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div>Kevin</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Jan 14, 2015 at 1:37 AM, &#39;Stéphane Laurent&#39; via packrat-discuss <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">packrat...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
