   "subject": "Re: collaboration between a Linux user and a Windows user",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<p dir=\"ltr\">Correct me if I&#39;m wrong, but BioC versions are tightly bound to R versions--BioC 2.14 only works with R 3.1. So I think the problem actually is that you both need to run the same version of R.</p>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r\n<div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Jan 14, 2015 11:55 AM, &quot;&#39;Stéphane Laurent&#39; via packrat-discuss&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">packrat...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br type=\"attribution\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hello Kevin, <div><br></div><div> I think the packrat.lock file should be splitted into two files, as below. The first part is user-specific : a difference between Packrat version, R version, links to repos, is not extremely important for collaborating.  The second part containing the packages versions is extremely important for collaboration.</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#606\">PackratFormat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.4</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">PackratVersion</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">RVersion</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3.1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Repos</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> CRAN</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">http</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#800\">//<a href=\"http://cran.rstudio.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://cran.rstudio.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242674102000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3RBNYTBXmtL9e65mKZ9CG6\">cran.rstudio.com</a>,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#606\">BioCsoft</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">http</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#800\">//<a href=\"http://bioconductor.org/packages/2.14/bioc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://bioconductor.org/packages/2.14/bioc&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242674102000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1RdrZrvRkDXYZpXyiPQVVv\">bioconductor.org/packages/2.14/bioc</a>,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#606\">BioCann</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">http</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#800\">//<a href=\"http://bioconductor.org/packages/2.14/data/annotation\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://bioconductor.org/packages/2.14/data/annotation&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242674102000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1Gth9C_Io61JZEXhWdwkMd\">bioconductor.org/packages/2.14/data/annotation</a>,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#606\">BioCexp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">http</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#800\">//<a href=\"http://bioconductor.org/packages/2.14/data/experiment\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://bioconductor.org/packages/2.14/data/experiment&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242674102000&amp;usg=AOvVaw37TR6GEmyLE_RbRdulmtJZ\">bioconductor.org/packages/2.14/data/experiment</a>,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#606\">BioCextra</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">http</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#800\">//<a href=\"http://bioconductor.org/packages/2.14/extra\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://bioconductor.org/packages/2.14/extra&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242674102000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2k2Cphvks6xfdJHarl7GiP\">bioconductor.org/packages/2.14/extra</a></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>___________</span><font color=\"#666600\"><span style=\"color:#000\"> SPLIT HERE __________<br></span></font><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Package</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> abind<br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Source</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> CRAN<br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Version</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Hash</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">5007322a6d081332d1d54b077a82bdf0</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Package</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">....</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span></div></code></div><div><br><br></div><div>Stéphane</div><div><br></div><br>Le mercredi 14 janvier 2015 20:11:16 UTC+1, Kevin Ushey a écrit :<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Stéphane,<div><br></div><div>The issue here appears to be incompatible BioC versions. Notice the paths generated:</div><div><br></div><div>    <i style=\"font-size:13px\"><a href=\"http://bioconductor.org/packages/2.14/bioc/bin/windows/contrib/3.0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://bioconductor.org/packages/2.14/bioc/bin/windows/contrib/3.0&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242674102000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1V7GLITe5gfVwSYGjOn7OK\">http://bioconductor.org/<u></u>packages/2.14/bioc/bin/<u></u>windows/contrib/3.0</a></i></div><div><br></div><div>The base comes from Packrat, and has 2.14, but is completed with 3.0. I imagine this is because we are seeing an incorrect version of BiocInstaller on the path?</div><div><br></div><div>I think a fix would involve us manually constructing these URLs, I think, and only respecting what we see in the Packrat lockfile -- but let me know if you can think of a local workaround as well.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div>Kevin</div></div><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Jan 14, 2015 at 1:37 AM, &#39;Stéphane Laurent&#39; via packrat-discuss <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">packrat...@googlegroups.<u></u>com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hello, <div><br></div><div>I&#39;m using Linux and I&#39;m collaborating with a Windows user (using Git). </div><div><br></div><div>We have done a first attempt to use packrat. I am the initiator. My <b>packrat.lock</b> file contains :</div><div><br></div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><div><i>Repos: CRAN=<a href=\"http://cran.rstudio.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://cran.rstudio.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242674102000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3RBNYTBXmtL9e65mKZ9CG6\">http://cran.rstudio.com</a>,</i></div></div><div><div><i>    BioCsoft=<a href=\"http://bioconductor.org/packages/2.14/bioc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://bioconductor.org/packages/2.14/bioc&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242674102000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1R